# mods.load — the game module list, read by nd_mods_load() at boot.
#
# One module per line. `#` starts a comment; blank lines are skipped.
#
# A line is one of three things
#   - a bare name WITH a module in this tree, loaded as `mods/<n>/<n>`, or
#   - a bare name WITHOUT one, which names an INSTALLED library by soname --
#     xy_load() appends the suffix and dlopen() resolves it through the normal
#     search path, so installing the package is all that is needed,
#   - a path (anything containing a `/`), taken VERBATIM -- which is how a
#     checkout is named without being copied into this tree. Nothing in the
#     tracked list uses this form any more; it survives for a module that is
#     still built in place, and `make mods` drives it by delegating to that
#     directory's own Makefile.
#
# Makefile's `mods:` target applies the identical test for the first two, so
# build and load never disagree about what a bare name means.
#
# Name the STEM, not the file: xy_load() appends `.so` itself, so a line
# `libnd-level.so` makes the engine look for `libnd-level.so.so` and fail. It
# also must be the INSTALLED FILENAME, with the `lib` prefix, not the bare
# module stem: module_load_path() appends `.so` and realpath()s, with no
# `lib`-prefix fallback and no soname fallback, so `libnd-level` resolves to
# libnd-level.so and `nd-level` would look for a file that is not installed.
#
# Lines that name a module which is not built are reported on stderr
# ("nd_mods_load: module ... failed to load"); the engine still boots.
demo
# Phase 1 vertical slice (MODS.md §6) and Phase 2 Wave 1 (MODS.md §7). Every
# one of these is now an installed library, so each is a bare name naming its
# soname: no module has an entry in this tree, and `make mods` therefore has
# nothing to build -- installing the package is the whole build step.
libnd-core
libnd-other
libnd-level
libnd-vanilla
# nd-shop is loaded AFTER nd-core because it registers an icon decorator with
# it: nd-core is the sole owner of on_icon and walks its decorator table in
# registration order, so a decorator loaded first would have nowhere to
# register. shop's own xy_install also xy_load()s nd-core by the same soname,
# which is a no-op refcount bump: module_load_path() realpath()s, so both
# spellings collapse to one entry.
libnd-shop
# nd-wts, nd-stone and nd-biome are ported and packaged but not loaded yet
# (MODS.md §9). Uncomment when there are assertions for them -- they are the
# three Wave 1 leaves with no firing site of their own.
#libnd-wts
#libnd-stone
#libnd-biome
# Phase 3 (all-19 port). Load order is dependency order AND chain order: a
# co-implementor must run after its chain base so nd_last() reads the base
# value. attr before race/class/equip/spell (attr_stat, effect, hp_max, mp_max
# chains); race before equip (wielded weapon overrides racial weight, and an
# unarmed equip passes the racial value through); fight before seat before
# spell (on_will_attack: fight builds the hit, seat stands up and passes it,
# spell amends with strikes).
libnd-attr
libnd-mortal
libnd-race
libnd-class
libnd-fight
libnd-drink
libnd-equip
libnd-seat
libnd-plant
libnd-mob
libnd-spell
../axil-nd-testprobe/testprobe
